messages:
maria: Kickoff: LineaBank wants a 2-week POC to prove we can act as a direct drop-in replacement for FastGenAPI (their current vendor). Key asks: identical request shape, predictable finish_reason mapping, and a parity report on 200 bank-specific prompts. Can we do dedicated+adapter?
ben: Yes. We can stand up a small Dedicated cluster and run a shim that accepts FastGenAPI endpoints and translates to Redwood payloads. Biggest items: default param differences (top_p, stop semantics) and metadata keys (they expect `meta.trace_id`).
sam: For the parity run, I'll use the lab harness and add 4 buckets: short replies, policy/filtering cases, multi-turn forms, and CSV/table extraction. We'll compute three metrics: n-gram overlap, hallucination incidents (manual triage), and structural field fidelity.
maria: Customer question: pricing for the POC and for an expected steady-state of ~50 rps during peak. They want a committed monthly rate option.
 en: rough numbers: POC (2x A100 equiv dedicated) ~ $7k/week including network. For steady-state 50 rps we should model 24/7 vs business hours; give them committed baseline and per-token carveouts. I'll draft an MSD with committed units + burst pricing.
junaid: Security front: they sent a vendor risk form. Need SOC2 type II, encryption at rest (KMS/HSM), subprocessor list, and the ability to keep logs in eu-north-1. Also: they require a signed DPA with data residency clause. I can compile answers but need a copy of their questionnaire PDF.
alexa: infra constraints: if LineaBank insists on VPC + customer-managed KMS, bootstrap takes ~6 business days for Private control plane. For POC we can either: (A) Shared-tenant dedicated with strict network ACLs, or (B) expedited private trial (adds time). Recommend A unless legal insists.
maria: small functional detail they flagged: FastGenAPI returns arrays of chunks with reasons like `stopped`/`truncated`. Their downstream pipelines look for `truncated` specifically. Can adapter normalize to our `finish_reason` values?
sam: yes. Adapter will map our finish_reason values to their expected enum. Also ensure streaming chunk shapes match (they use `chunk_id` and `chunk_index`). We'll fake those fields in the shim for parity.
ben: sample Node adapter route (Express):
```js
// POST /v1/fg/generate -> translate to Redwood call
app.post('/v1/fg/generate', async (req,res)=>{
  const {prompt,max_tokens} = req.body;
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/completions',{
    method:'POST',
    headers:{'Authorization':`Bearer ${process.env.RW}`},
    body: JSON.stringify({input: prompt, max_new_tokens: max_tokens, temperature:0.7})
  });
  const data = await r.json();
  // map fields to FastGenAPI shape
  const mapped = {chunks:[{chunk_id: '1', chunk_index:0, text: data.output[0].text, reason: data.finish_reason === 'stop' ? 'stopped' : data.finish_reason}]};
  res.json(mapped);
});
```
junaid: Good. Also call out telemetry: we must not send customer prompt text to any analytics outside their region. For Private control plane we can disable telemetry; for shared-tenant we need an agreement that masked logs are okay.
alexa: CI/ops note: provisioning ticket created if we go private: #PROV-4421. If shared-tenant, we just create project and allocate capacity.
ci-bot: Pipeline triggered: fg-adapter/lineabank -> staging. 6 checks running.
maria: timeline proposed: Day0: legal & questionnaire exchange, infra decision. Days 1-4: adapter prototype + parity harness prep. Days 5-9: run parity (200 prompts) + collect diffs. Days 10-14: remediation, demo, security review. Any objections?
 en: suggest adding a day for unexpected mapping issues. If customer insists on VPC, shift timeline +5 days.
sam: action items: (1) maria: get vendor questionnaire and prompt corpus from LineaBank, (2) ben: start adapter scaffold, (3) junaid: begin security answers, (4) alexa: confirm infra path. We'll sync EOD Friday.
maria: I'll email the customer for the questionnaire and their security contact (secops@lineabank.com). Thanks all :rocket:
